<button class="filter-btn" data-filter="Digital">Digital</button>
<button class="filter-btn" data-filter="Research">Research</button></div>
    <div class="grid grid-3"><div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Sales"><span class="tag">Sales</span><h3>How to plan long term by estimating industry size five years out</h3><p>An Alco-Bev major wanted to size categories like Whisky and Vodka five years into the future. RainMan built an ARIMA-plus model over 15 years of SKU-level sales, adding environmental data such as per-capita income and demographic growth for a more realistic estimate in a fast-evolving market.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Research"><span class="tag">Research</span><h3>Using geo-targeting to improve lift from digital</h3><p>A healthcare brand needed to size investment across digital channels. RainMan clustered markets, built a low-MAPE model predicting one market from others, then ran a channel-by-channel lift experiment — letting ROI be compared and spend optimized across key digital channels.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Digital"><span class="tag">Digital</span><h3>Paid, owned and earned media, and the path to sales</h3><p>A CPG brand couldn't see how paid, owned and earned media interacted. Econometric modelling found paid media drove 70% of sales-movement influence and 60% of awareness — with a resulting 12% ROI improvement across connect points.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Media"><span class="tag">Media</span><h3>Comparing offline and online returns to optimize spend</h3><p>A global cosmetics brand needed to arrest a sales decline across Asia. A proprietary quality-weighted Facebook impressions measure and linear regression identified digital, and Facebook specifically, as the leading driver — reallocating budget added an 8% lift in sales.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Sales"><span class="tag">Sales</span><h3>Reducing churn for a life insurance company with a predictive model</h3><p>A logistic regression model scored policyholders on demographics, environmental factors and payment behaviour to predict lapse and surrender. 90% of actual lapsers fell in the top three risk deciles, giving the insurer a robust way to target retention.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Retail"><span class="tag">Retail</span><h3>Clustering to predict jewellery sales at a store level</h3><p>A jewellery chain needed to optimize inventory and new-product indents per store. Clustering stores by items sold, type, days-to-sell and quantity produced four store types, each with its own replenishment rules — lowering inventory while lifting sales.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Sales"><span class="tag">Sales</span><h3>Keeping a hardware major's sales team from wasting time</h3><p>A 20-person key-account team covering 9,000 accounts needed sharper targeting. A Cox Proportional Hazards model scored the probability of each client buying a given product at a given time — lifting successful sales calls above 90% and overall sales by close to 20%.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Sales"><span class="tag">Sales</span><h3>Easing a salesman's burden with predictive SKU lists</h3><p>Field sales reps struggled to scroll hundreds of SKUs on handheld devices. RainMan's probability-scoring model narrowed each store's list to its highest-probability SKUs, correctly predicting 90% of what stores actually bought and lifting cross-sell.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Marketing"><span class="tag">Marketing</span><h3>Making promotions work for your brand</h3><p>A consumer goods major needed to know which value and volume promotions actually worked. A customised marketing mix model measured contribution by discount depth, publicity and duration — streamlining spend while delivering higher sales.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Marketing"><span class="tag">Marketing</span><h3>Pricing analytics: optimizing price to lift sales value</h3><p>Moving price-elasticity analysis from brand level down to pack and category level uncovered differentiated pricing opportunities — adding up to 6% margin for a food major, and letting a menswear retailer safely raise prices on select categories.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Marketing"><span class="tag">Marketing</span><h3>The long-term ad effect that changed a personal-care strategy</h3><p>Long-term effects of advertising, quantified through MMM, reshaped how a leading personal-care brand thought about sustained media investment versus short-term activation.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Research"><span class="tag">Research</span><h3>Turning brand-health data into marketing action</h3><p>Connecting continuous brand-tracking data to sales and share outcomes gave the marketing team a clear read on which brand-health metrics actually moved the business.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Media"><span class="tag">Media</span><h3>Lifting FMCG marketing effectiveness by over 15%</h3><p>Rather than budget by habit, a top FMCG food brand built 14+ market-level models to find its real sales drivers. Shifting spend from underperforming BTL into TV and high-ROI growth markets more than doubled sales growth without changing the total budget.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Media"><span class="tag">Media</span><h3>Arresting decline and boosting profitability for a consumer goods brand</h3><p>Multivariate regression with Bayesian shrinkage isolated distribution, creative and pricing as the priority levers for a declining Asia brand — lifting marketing ROI by 20% across market clusters.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Creative"><span class="tag">Creative</span><h3>How long can a creative copy sustain response?</h3><p>Econometric modelling with Kalman-filtered ad-stock decomposition measured copy wear-out across 18 creative variants — the best copy decayed at 12% a month, others at 18%, guiding an optimal creative rotation strategy.</p></div>
<div class="card case-card show" data-cat="Digital"><span class="tag">Digital</span><h3>What is the impact of the online medium on sales?</h3><p>A deep dive into online media's direct and indirect contribution to sales, isolating its true incremental effect from that of other channels in the mix.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

